{
  "program": "COUSR01C",
  "caseId": "case17",
  "description": "WHEN OTHER on the AID - app/cbl/COUSR01C.cbl:98-102 - reached by a key that resolves to nothing at all. DFHPA3 is x'6B', and it is the interesting one: app/cpy/CSSTRPFY.cpy tests twenty-eight AIDs and DFHPA3 is not among them, even though DFHPA1 and DFHPA2 immediately before it are, so common.PfKeyResolver returns no key whatsoever for it. The source EVALUATE in CSSTRPFY has no WHEN OTHER and does not pre-clear CCARD-AID, which is exactly why 'no key' is a distinct answer from 'some key this program does not name' - and case18 takes that other route. Either way COUSR01C:98-102 answers, and the arm does THREE things rather than two: it raises WS-ERR-FLG at :99, it moves -1 into FNAMEL at :100, and it moves CCDA-MSG-INVALID-KEY at :101. That message is app/cpy/CSMSG01Y.cpy's literal reproduced byte for byte in common.SystemMessages - forty characters of text and ten trailing spaces, fifty in all, before the MOVE to WS-MESSAGE pads it to eighty. EIBAID is tested inline in this program: COUSR01C is one of the twelve that do not COPY CSSTRPFY, and the single shared resolver must reproduce those inline tests as identical boolean outcomes.",
